d:["$","section",null,{"id":"strategies","className":"mb-12 scroll-mt-32","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Test-taking strategies"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 max-w-[68ch] text-lg leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-600","children":"These apply to every passage, regardless of the question type."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","article","Return to the passage every time",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Return to the passage every time"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"The single largest source of avoidable errors is answering from memory after one read. On a reading test, the passage is open in front of you and rechecking it is free. Any question that names a paragraph, quotes a phrase, or asks what a word means is telling you exactly where to look."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-2 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-4","children":[["$","li","Read the question and identify what it points you to.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Read the question and identify what it points you to."}]]}],["$","li","Go back and read that part, plus one sentence on either side.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Go back and read that part, plus one sentence on either side."}]]}],["$","li","Answer from what you just read, not from what you remember.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Answer from what you just read, not from what you remember."}]]}]]}]]}],["$","article","Predict before you look at the choices",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Predict before you look at the choices"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"Well-written wrong answers are designed to look reasonable. The most reliable defense is to decide what you think before you see them. Cover the choices, answer the question in your own words, then uncover them and find the closest match."}],"$undefined"]}],["$","article","Eliminate rather than select",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Eliminate rather than select"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"When two choices both look plausible, stop trying to pick the winner and start disqualifying. Most wrong answers on a reading test fail in one of four predictable ways, and naming the failure is faster than defending the answer you like."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-2 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-4","children":[["$","li","Too narrow — true, but it covers only part of the passage.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],"$L1b"]}],"$L1c","$L1d","$L1e"]}]]}],"$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22"]}]]}]
