1f:["$","article","Find the textual evidence before you commit",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Find the textual evidence before you commit"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"Before you fill in an answer, finish this sentence: \"I know this because the passage says ______.\" If you cannot complete it with actual words from the text, you are guessing. That does not always mean the answer is wrong, but it tells you which questions to revisit if you have time left."}],"$undefined"]}]
20:["$","article","Pace yourself, and use the whole time",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Pace yourself, and use the whole time"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"Running out of time and rushing the last passage costs more points than a single hard question ever will. A steady pace with a plan for hard items protects your score better than speed."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"mt-4 space-y-2 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-4","children":[["$","li","Check the clock after the first passage and see whether your pace fits the section.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Check the clock after the first passage and see whether your pace fits the section."}]]}],["$","li","Give a genuinely hard question one honest attempt, then mark it and move on.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Give a genuinely hard question one honest attempt, then mark it and move on."}]]}],["$","li","Never leave an answer blank — an eliminated-down guess is better than nothing.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Never leave an answer blank — an eliminated-down guess is better than nothing."}]]}],["$","li","Spend leftover time on the questions you marked, not on re-reading answers you were confident about.",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-eng-teal-600","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Spend leftover time on the questions you marked, not on re-reading answers you were confident about."}]]}]]}]]}]
21:["$","article","Read the passage before the questions",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Read the passage before the questions"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"Some test-takers try to save time by reading the questions first. For TABE Reading, a single focused read of the passage first is usually faster overall, because most questions require a sense of the whole text. Read for the main idea and the shape of the passage, and do not try to memorize details — you can look those up."}],"$undefined"]}]
22:["$","article","Watch for absolute words",{"className":"rounded-2xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Watch for absolute words"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":"Words such as always, never, all, every, and only make a statement much harder to support. They are not automatically wrong, but a choice containing one needs evidence that is just as absolute. When you see one, go find that evidence specifically."}],"$undefined"]}]
